CONCEPT
  product:   Stevedore
  one-liner: Frontend infrastructure for developers named Steve, resolved by middle initial.
  The joke is namespace collision. Every user is called Steve, so the platform's hardest
  engineering problem is telling its own customers apart, and it solves that with a permanent
  numeric suffix it refuses to show them.

DESIGN DIRECTION
  style:   Supergraphic corporate identity manual, 1974, manual-stock daylight mode.
           Full-bleed colour bands opened by CSS quarter-circle arcs, clause numbering
           (1.0 / 2.1 / PLATE 03), roundel identity mark reused as bullet, badge and
           portrait frame. Zero shadows, zero radii on plates, flat floods only.
  palette: primary #0E5C55 identity teal (sole carrier) · accent #8E2434 oxblood
           (quarantined to identity telemetry: contested Steves, low confidence,
           the coin-flip line) · bg #F6EDDC · fg/ink #1A1712 · muted #8C8069
  fonts:   display Jost · body Newsreader · mono Space Mono (tabular figures)
  anti-sameness: checked against the last 7 entries (tesla-for-hedgehogs,
           instagram-for-plant-parents, lyft-for-ferrets, venmo-for-retired-racehorses,
           instagram-for-wolves, figma-for-left-handed-people, replit-for-red-pandas).
           No collision on style, palette or font pair. Jost, Newsreader and Space Mono
           have not been used in that window; teal + oxblood on cream is unused.
           The ui-ux-pro-max design-system query returned the generic dev-tool default
           (OLED dark, JetBrains Mono, #0F172A/#22C55E), which would have collided with
           two dark entries in the window, so the palette and pairing were derived instead.

